# /etc/default/slothweb — site configuration for slothweb.service (#153).
#
# Read by systemd as an EnvironmentFile: KEY=value, one per line, no
# shell expansion and no quoting. `make install-service` installs this
# file only when there is none, so an edited copy is never replaced.
#
# The unit fixes the three paths (--socket unix:/run/sloth/sloth.sock,
# --sloth-db /var/lib/sloth/sloth.db, --store /var/lib/slothweb/
# slothweb.db); the sandbox admits no others, so they do not go here.
#
# Empty, slothweb listens on 127.0.0.1:8770 and admits loopback peers
# only. Reach it from another machine with an SSH tunnel:
#   ssh -L 8770:127.0.0.1:8770 sensor-host
#
# Binding a Tailscale address instead. Every flag is needed, and each is
# refused on its own: a non-loopback --web-bind needs --web-allow-remote,
# and --web-allow-remote admits no peer you did not name. Name exactly
# one viewer, as a /32. The addresses below are placeholders from the
# Tailscale range, not any real host; use `tailscale ip -4` on the
# sensor for the bind and on the viewer for the --web-allow.
#
#   --web-bind 100.64.0.10:8770     this host's own Tailscale address
#   --web-allow-remote              authorise the non-loopback bind
#   --web-allow 100.64.0.20/32      the one machine that may view it
#
# Loopback stays admitted whatever the bind, and a connection the host
# makes to its own address from 127.0.0.1 is a loopback peer: that is
# how `sloth-migrate-sensor --with-slothweb` reads /api/health on the
# bound address without a second --web-allow entry
# (curl --interface 127.0.0.1 http://100.64.0.10:8770/api/health).
#
# Do not add `tailscale serve` or a funnel in front of it.
#
# The alert page's packet capture (web/README.md "An alert's proof"):
# the sensor's --pcap-dir, read in place. /var/lib/sloth is already
# read-only in the unit's sandbox, so nothing else needs widening. Only
# files named as sloth names alert pcaps are opened, never a handshake
# pcap or eapol.22000. An evidence pcap from the sensor's --eapol-dir
# is listed but withheld (it may hold EAPOL/PMKID handshake material)
# unless --web-serve-evidence-pcap is added; with --web-allow-remote
# that is refused unless spelled --web-serve-evidence-pcap=remote.
#   --pcap-dir /var/lib/sloth/pcap
#
# Example:
#   SLOTHWEB_ARGS=--web-bind 100.64.0.10:8770 --web-allow-remote --web-allow 100.64.0.20/32
#   SLOTHWEB_ARGS=--pcap-dir /var/lib/sloth/pcap
SLOTHWEB_ARGS=
